description: Layer and project structure so UI, domain, and storage stay replaceable
alwaysApply: true
---

# Layers

One desktop product. Swap the UI or the database engine without rewriting domain logic.

**C# projects** (WinUI 3 / Windows App SDK):

- `Atten.Core` — leave, sheet, dates, validation. No UI, SQLite, or file paths.
- `Atten.Data` — repository, migrations, connection, backup. No windows, colors, or controls.
- `Atten.UI.Theme` — tokens and `App*` controls. No business rules, SQL, or Data. May reference `Atten.Core` only for dates (format, parse, month days).
- `Atten.App` — feature screens and `Shared` pickers. Calls services only. No SQL, `PRAGMA`, or `atten.db` paths.

Pages read and write only through services or the repository. `data/atten.db`, WAL, and file snapshots stay in the data/connection layer (`src/Atten.Data`).

Domain tests must pass without opening a window.

A later UI toolkit change touches only App and Theme. A later PostgreSQL move touches only Data.
